# Email templates (Golf Sol Ireland)

All customer-facing transactional mail shares one **640px table-based shell**: turf background (`#F4F7F5`), dark emerald hero (`gs.dark`), gold accent bar, **white main card** for message body, optional **marketing tail** (fleet / tiles / trust / green CTA), then **dark footer** with logo, contacts, company reg, disclaimer. Logo sizes are centralized as **`EMAIL_LOGO_HEADER_W` / `EMAIL_LOGO_HEADER_H`** (top bar) and **`EMAIL_LOGO_HERO_W` / `EMAIL_LOGO_HERO_H`** (hero lockup) in [branded-email-shell.mjs](mdc:server/branded-email-shell.mjs); keep [branded-enquiry-email.mjs](mdc:server/branded-enquiry-email.mjs) in sync when you change them.

## Source of truth (read before editing)

| Layer | File | Responsibility |
|--------|------|------------------|
| Visual system + primitives | [branded-email-shell.mjs](mdc:server/branded-email-shell.mjs) | `gs` palette, `emailFonts`, `escapeHtml`, `ctaGold` / `ctaGreen`, `assetUrl`, `buildBrandedEmailHeadAndOpen`, `buildBrandedPreheaderThroughHeaderRow`, `buildBrandedMarketingTailHtml`, `buildBrandedFooterHtml`, **`buildBrandedTransactionalEmailHtml`** |
| Finalize + browser preview | [email-layout.mjs](mdc:server/email-layout.mjs) | `buildGsolTransactionalEmail`, **`finalizeGsolEmailHtml`** (terms/social), `adaptTransactionalEmailHtmlForBrowserPreview` |
| Brand lines + legacy CID keys (preview only) | [email-constants.mjs](mdc:server/email-constants.mjs) | `gsolEmailBrand`, `gsolCompanyLegal`, optional `logoLockupEmailContentId` / `socialContentIds` for old HTML preview |
| Enquiry customer/admin HTML | [branded-enquiry-email.mjs](mdc:server/branded-enquiry-email.mjs) | Full document duplicated from the shell visual system — update alongside `branded-email-shell.mjs` when changing header/hero chrome. |

Feature emails import **`buildGsolTransactionalEmail`** + **`finalizeGsolEmailHtml`** from [email-layout.mjs](mdc:server/email-layout.mjs) (see [branded-transfer-payment-email.mjs](mdc:server/branded-transfer-payment-email.mjs), [branded-client-portal-email.mjs](mdc:server/branded-client-portal-email.mjs), [transfer-booking-notify-service.mjs](mdc:server/transfer-booking-notify-service.mjs), etc.).

## Mandatory patterns

1. **Layout**: nested `<table role="presentation">`, **inline styles** on cells; MSO conditional wrappers are already in `buildBrandedEmailHeadAndOpen` — do not strip them.
2. **Typography / colour**: use **`emailFonts.sans`** and **`gs.*`** tokens from [branded-email-shell.mjs](mdc:server/branded-email-shell.mjs) in new fragments so mail stays on-brand.
3. **User-controlled text** (names, routes, IDs): escape with **`escapeHtml()`** from [branded-email-shell.mjs](mdc:server/branded-email-shell.mjs) before interpolating into HTML. Hero copy that embeds user data must be safe.
4. **Main card body**: pass **`bodyHtml`** / **`mainCardInnerHtml`** as HTML you control. If you only have `<tr>...</tr>` fragments, the shell normalizes them via **`normalizeTransactionalEmailBodyHtml`**.
5. **Sending through Resend**: build raw HTML, then run **`finalizeGsolEmailHtml(html)`** so `/terms-and-conditions` and optional **`GSOL-SOCIAL-ICONS`** placeholders resolve (brand logos in HTML already use **`assetUrl`** — no image attachments). For iframe dev preview, use **`adaptTransactionalEmailHtmlForBrowserPreview`** from [email-layout.mjs](mdc:server/email-layout.mjs).
6. **Preheader**: short inbox preview string; keep aligned with `heroLead` / subject.
7. **Footer disclaimer**: pass **`footerDisclaimerHtml`** into `buildBrandedTransactionalEmailHtml` when the default admin copy in `buildBrandedFooterHtml` is wrong for the mail type.
8. **Mobile (`@media only screen and (max-width: 680px)`)**: keep [branded-email-shell.mjs](mdc:server/branded-email-shell.mjs) and [branded-enquiry-email.mjs](mdc:server/branded-enquiry-email.mjs) **in lockstep**. Patterns: **`email-outer-shell`** trims outer padding; **`email-header-row`** stacks logo → tagline → phone with **`email-header-phone-link`** tap target; **`email-hero-logo`** scales in hero; **`email-tile-row` / `email-tile-cell`** add vertical rhythm when three tiles stack; **`email-trust-badge` / `email-trust-body`** stack trust row; fluid **`img`** under `.email-shell`; **`#MessageViewBody`** width for Gmail webview quirks.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ External CSS only, or `<div>`-first layouts without tables — breaks Outlook.
- ❌ Unescaped DB fields or Stripe metadata in HTML strings.
- ❌ Calling Resend without **`finalizeGsolEmailHtml`** on the Golf Sol transactional shell (`href="/terms-and-conditions"` and social placeholder fixes will be wrong).
- ❌ Duplicating the full `<html>…` shell in a new module — extend **`buildGsolTransactionalEmail`** / **`buildBrandedTransactionalEmailHtml`** instead.

## Canonical builder flow (Resend)

```javascript
import { buildGsolTransactionalEmail, finalizeGsolEmailHtml } from './email-layout.mjs'
import { emailFonts, escapeHtml, gs } from './branded-email-shell.mjs'

const subject = 'Golf Sol Ireland — example'
const htmlRaw = buildGsolTransactionalEmail({
  documentTitle: subject,
  preheader: 'Short preview line for the inbox.',
  heroKicker: 'Golf Sol Ireland',
  heroTitle: 'Headline in the hero',
  heroLead: 'Supporting sentence under the headline.',
  heroMetaHtml: `<p style="margin:0;">Optional meta strip (HTML-safe)</p>`,
  bodyHtml: `<p style="margin:0;font-family:${emailFonts.sans};font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:${gs.text};">Hello ${escapeHtml(customerName)}, …</p>`
})
const html = finalizeGsolEmailHtml(htmlRaw)
// send with Resend — brand images use absolute SITE_URL links in HTML; PDFs attach separately when needed
```

## Layout reference (same shell as live mail)

[branded-sample-document-html.mjs](mdc:server/branded-sample-document-html.mjs) exports **`getBrandedSampleDocumentPreviewHtml()`** — full HTML using **`buildBrandedTransactionalEmailHtml`** with fictional body content. Use it for PDF/print alignment and visual QA. Dev route: [email-template-preview.tsx](mdc:src/pages/email-template-preview.tsx) (`/email-template-preview`).

## Optional: social strip placeholder

Templates may include the HTML comment pair **`<!-- GSOL-SOCIAL-ICONS -->` … `<!-- /GSOL-SOCIAL-ICONS -->`** in the string passed to **`finalizeGsolEmailHtml`** (see [email-layout.mjs](mdc:server/email-layout.mjs)); the finalizer replaces it with **text links** (LinkedIn, Facebook, WhatsApp, Bluesky) — **no PNG attachments**.
